-- #1110 origin-agreement corpus — the RESIDUAL section's POSITIVE CONTROL.
--
-- The `graph` fixture beside this one produces a residual with ZERO `graph` rows:
-- every head the graph driver saw acquired an identity. That is a good result, but
-- ON ITS OWN IT IS NOT READABLE — an empty arm is exactly what a section that
-- CANNOT emit that arm would also print, and "the check that reported green was
-- structurally unable to report anything else" is the failure this whole gate
-- exists to prevent. A reviewer looking at the other golden cannot tell the two
-- apart.
--
-- So this fixture makes the graph arm's residual NON-EMPTY on purpose. `Missing` is
-- declared nowhere, in no module and not in the prelude, so it is resolve.mdk's
-- residual case (1): "the name is in no scope at all". `checkType` reports it as
-- `UnknownType`, errors ACCUMULATE rather than exiting, so the tree still reaches
-- the stamper — which correctly leaves the head `OriginUnresolved`, because there
-- is no module to attribute it to. The golden pins `graph main_unresolved Missing`.
--
-- ⚠️ THAT ROW IS THE CONTROL, NOT A BUG. Deleting `Missing` to "fix" the gate
-- disarms the control and silently returns the residual section to unfalsifiable.
-- If this row ever disappears, the question is what stopped emitting it.
--
-- ⚠️ It must ALSO stay a graph-arm row specifically. The flat and single arms are
-- silent about far more (see the probe's residual section comment), so a residual
-- row from either of them proves nothing about the graph arm's ability to speak.
--
-- One module, no imports: the control needs a head the GRAPH path cannot attribute,
-- and adding a module graph around it would only enlarge the golden.

data Parcel = Parcel Int

parcelSize : Parcel -> Int
parcelSize (Parcel n) = n

-- The control itself. `Missing` is intentionally undeclared.
labelOf : Parcel -> Missing
labelOf _ = panic "control fixture: never evaluated"

main = println (parcelSize (Parcel 3))
